- Modified getMyRooms() to include userId in query parameters
- Modified getRoomsOverview() to include userId in query parameters
- Updated to match backend API specification requiring userId parameter

The API URLs now include userId:
- /chat/rooms/my?userId={userId}&page={page}&size={size}
- /chat/rooms/overview?userId={userId}

Addresses insufficient bounds checking in `get_dhcp_server_identifier()` when parsing DHCP options. The existing check at line 918 only validates reading option type and length, but doesn't prevent out-of-bounds access during memcpy or when skipping option data.

## Changes

- Add bounds check before `memcpy(&server_ip, &offer_packet->options[itr1], sizeof(struct in_addr))` to ensure `itr1 + sizeof(struct in_addr) <= MAX_DHCP_OPTIONS_LENGTH`
- Add bounds check before incrementing `itr1` by `option_length` to prevent index overflow when skipping option data

```c
if(option_type==DHCP_OPTION_SERVER_IDENTIFIER)
{
    if (itr1 + sizeof(struct in_addr) > MAX_DHCP_OPTIONS_LENGTH) break;
    memcpy(&server_ip, &offer_packet->options[itr1], sizeof(struct in_addr));
    return server_ip.s_addr;
}
else
{
    if (itr1 + option_length > MAX_DHCP_OPTIONS_LENGTH) break;
    for(itr2=0;itr2<(int)option_length;itr2++,itr1++);
}
```

Also adds `.gitignore` for autotools build artifacts.

